---
source: crates/fossil-graph/tests/schemas.rs
expression: "schema_for! (aggregate::AggregateParams)"
---
$schema: "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#"
title: AggregateParams
description: "One grouping, over values or over ranges.\n\n**Binning is grouping**, which is why `histogram` is not a second verb: it was the same `GROUP BY` with the key computed from a range instead of read from a column. Setting [`Self::bins`] is what picks which, and it is the only difference between the two."
type: object
required:
  - agg
  - group_by
  - vertex_type
properties:
  agg:
    $ref: "#/definitions/Aggregation"
  bins:
    description: "Group over this many equal-width ranges of `group_by` rather than over its distinct values — what `histogram` used to be. Requires a numeric or temporal column: a categorical one has no ranges, and grouping it by value is already the answer."
    default: ~
    type:
      - integer
      - "null"
    format: uint32
    minimum: 0
  group_by:
    description: "The column the groups come from — its values, or its ranges when [`Self::bins`] is set."
    type: string
  limit:
    description: "Cap on rows returned. Groups are ordered by value and cut here; a binned call is cut to this many bins instead, so `limit` means one thing."
    default: 1000
    type: integer
    format: uint32
    minimum: 0
  measure:
    description: "Optional measure column for `sum`/`avg`/`min`/`max` aggregations. Ignored when `agg` is `count`."
    default: ~
    type:
      - string
      - "null"
  vertex_type:
    type: string
additionalProperties: false
definitions:
  Aggregation:
    type: string
    enum:
      - count
      - sum
      - avg
      - min
      - max
